 n uncovers what appears to be Verity's chilling autobiographical notes\, s
 he wrestles with the disturbing and twisted confessions about Verity’s h
 usband Jeremy (Josh Hartnett)\, and finds it hard to separate fiction from
  reality\, manipulation from attraction\, and opportunity from obsession.\
